---
import GuideLayout from '@layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
import ReferenceBlock from '@components/ReferenceBlock.astro';
import { config } from './config';
import { withBase } from '@lib/paths';
import { categories } from '@data/categories';
import type { EcosystemEntry } from '@data/types';

interface Props {
  title: string;
  description: string;
  readMinutes: number;
  updatedAt: string;
  entry: EcosystemEntry;
}

const props = Astro.props;
const category = categories.find(c => c.slug === config.categorySlug)!;
const toolHref = withBase(`/tool/${category.segment}/${config.slug}/`);
---

<GuideLayout
  {...props}
  toolSlug={config.slug}
  toolName={config.name}
  toolCategorySlug={config.categorySlug}
>
  <section id="quick-answer">
    <h2>Quick Answer <span class="gold-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span></h2>
    <p>
      A breathing circle is a visual for inhale, hold, and exhale. This one names the pattern:
      Box (4-4-4-4), 4-7-8, or Coherent (5-5). Default is Box. There is no preset called Calm,
      because a calm label that runs a different timing is a lie.
    </p>
    <p>
      For example: Input: Box selected. Output: four seconds in, four hold, four out, four hold,
      with a phase name and a remaining-seconds count. Mute the soft cue if the room is shared.
    </p>
    <a href={toolHref} class="cta-link">Open Breathing Circle →</a>
  </section>

  <section id="what-is">
    <h2>What is a breathing circle? <span class="gold-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span></h2>
    <p>
      Meditation apps want an account. YouTube timers cannot change the pattern. A circle that
      expands on inhale and settles on exhale is the usual visual. The useful part is the timing
      you can read, not the glow.
    </p>
    <p>
      Box breathing is 4-4-4-4. 4-7-8 breathing is inhale 4, hold 7, exhale 8. Coherent breathing
      is an even 5-5. Pick one. The numbers sit on the button so the tool cannot hide what it is
      doing. This breathing exercise animation is a calm breathing visual and a breathing timer
      you can follow online without an account.
    </p>
    <ReferenceBlock type="key-idea" heading="Name the pattern">
      <p>
        If the default is labelled calm and runs faster than box, the user cannot tell what they
        are practising. Named presets with visible counts are the orientation this tool adds.
      </p>
    </ReferenceBlock>
  </section>

  <section id="session">
    <h2>How do I follow box breathing online? <span class="gold-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span></h2>
    <p>
      Open the tool, keep Box selected, and breathe with the counts. That is how to follow box
      breathing online in this tab. Mute breathing cues under the board or Settings → Feel when
      the room is shared. Sound and motion are independent, the same Feel contract as Pop It.
      Play session hides the rest of the page and uses the dark overlay surface. Exit or Escape
      restores the page. Native fullscreen is a bonus; if the browser refuses, the overlay stays.
    </p>
    <p>
      Reduced motion keeps the circle still. Phase name and seconds remain, so you can follow
      Box without the scale animation. A session ends with a fade, not a cut.
    </p>
    <ReferenceBlock type="common-mistake" heading="Leaving the cue on in an office">
      <p>
        The soft tone is optional. Mute once under Settings → Feel and every fidget, including
        this circle, stays quiet.
      </p>
    </ReferenceBlock>
  </section>

  <section id="common-mistakes">
    <h2>Common mistakes <span class="gold-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span></h2>
    <p>
      Trusting a calm label that is not a named pattern is the failure this page exists to
      avoid. Box is 4-4-4-4. 4-7-8 is 4, 7, and 8. Coherent is 5-5. Therefore you can read what
      you are practising.
    </p>
    <p>
      Leaving the cue on in an office is the other miss. Mute under Settings → Feel. Reduced
      motion does not end the session: the phase name and seconds still run.
    </p>
    <ReferenceBlock type="common-mistake" heading="Treating reduced motion as off">
      <p>
        The circle stops expanding. The counts do not. You can still finish a Box round.
      </p>
    </ReferenceBlock>
  </section>

  <section id="vs">
    <h2>Named presets vs a vague calm timer <span class="gold-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span></h2>
    <p>
      Named presets vs a vague calm timer is the point. No account, no subscription, no voice.
      The circle runs in the tab. You cannot change another site's YouTube timer. You can change
      Box to 4-7-8 breathing here in one tap. That is the whole difference that matters for a
      two-minute reset.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="try">
    <h2>Try a Box round <span class="gold-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span></h2>
    <p>
      Open the tool, confirm Box 4-4-4-4 is selected, mute if you need to, then Play session if
      you want the rest of the page gone. Exit when you are done.
    </p>
    <a href={toolHref} class="cta-link">Open Breathing Circle →</a>
  </section>
</GuideLayout>

<style>
  .cta-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    height: var(--touch-target);
    padding-inline: var(--space-5);
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
    background: var(--color-accent);
    color: var(--color-text-inverse);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: var(--transition-color);
  }
  .cta-link:hover { opacity: 0.9; text-decoration: none; }
</style>
